"""The rules factory (DECISIONS D58): rule targets generated by code from the law, read by two blind readers of different
families, recorded in the governance log; a rule settles only when the other family replicates the reading (D43).

    .venv/bin/python tools/rule_factory.py targets [--round N]   list the round's targets (no writing)
    .venv/bin/python tools/rule_factory.py prompts [--round N]   governance/readings/fabrica<N>/<rule>/prompt.json, fixed once written
    .venv/bin/python tools/rule_factory.py record [--round N]    propose or correct (leitor:a8) + blind review (leitor:b) -> log, rules/,
                                                                 FABRICA<N>.md

Round 2 (D60): the vocabulary grows by prazo_candidaturas_dias and data_envio_convite (read_rules round 8); its targets are
round 1's whose only gaps those values close, read again by both readers; a rule already in the log gets a correction.

Round 3 (D62): the person's vocabulary (read_rules round 9): urgencia_fundamentada, setores_especiais, anuncio_pre_informacao,
concurso_concecao / concurso_ideias with modalidade_concecao, the deadline prazo_trabalhos_concecao_dias, usual_days beside an
absolute minimum, and an answer that may hold up to three rules. Targets: round 1's with a gap this closes, and 190.º n.º 1 (two
rules in one passage). A target's second and third rules get ids ending -b, -c.

Round 6 (D66): the reading protocol v3 (tools/read_rules_v3.py): the target in its place in the law, the reading rules
in the prompt, every condition and parameter quoting its words; the checker decides which answers can be recorded. Two
readings replicate on their canonical content, or on the same «não tipável» reason, which settles an assertion of type
nao_tipavel and invalidates the target's proposed rules. `withdraw --rule ID --product-rule ID` invalidates one settled rule
a person's product rule takes out (D66: 88.º n.º 2 a)).

Recheck (D64): `recheck --round N` compares the answers a round recorded again under the person's product rule
product_rule:replicacao-conteudo-e-alvo (the same rule, both citing the target passage); a rule they now replicate gets
leitor:b's blind review again, from the same answer, as an uphold that names that rule. No reader is asked again.

Targets, round 1: the leaf passages of the CCP in force on 2026-10-01 that state, in their own words, a minimum number of
days for something to be done (prazo_minimo) or a value limit in euros (limiar) — the two rule types the engine evaluates
today. Articles already read by hand (19, 20, 135, 136: B3, D44-D51) are left out. The candidates are the passage's whole
article; the question asks for the rule the passage states. The readers' prompts and schemas are read_rules' (typed
conditions, round 3 on). A passage that states no such rule gives two readings that do not replicate: nothing settles.
"""
